HOMIO / REOS — PowerShell → GitHub Work Plan
Canonical repository: prajaktaranjane80-sketch/Homio
Canonical branch: reos-development
Canonical frontend root: REOS_CONTROL_CENTER/Frontend
Purpose: Make direct PowerShell-to-GitHub work safe, repeatable, and verifiable. Then continue real HOMIO work one part at a time.
Operating rules
1. GitHub branch reos-development is the source of truth. Do not treat a local checkout as canonical.
2. PowerShell is allowed to call GitHub APIs for the requested remote work. Do not write, patch, reset, merge, or push code through a local worktree.
3. Before every write, read the live branch head and the exact existing remote file. Never rely on a stale commit SHA.
4. A write must be guarded: create a commit whose parent is the expected live head; recheck the head before moving the branch; never force-update the branch.
5. After a write, independently read the remote commit and file/blob back. Record the commit URL, changed path, and verification evidence in REOS_CONTROL_CENTER/PS Output without claiming unverified PASS.
6. One part at a time. Do not make unrelated edits, duplicate files/engines, or rerun unrelated tests without reason.
7. AI_AGENT_ENTRYPOINT.py is the canonical agent-facing workflow policy and has been restored/aligned. Final ACRL policy/continuity alignment remains deferred until operational fixes are stable. Supporting plans must not contradict the EntryPoint.
